# Hartree-Fock geometry optimization of LiH with the optimizer thresholds pinned
# EXPLICITLY, rather than left to be derived.
#
# This is the companion to scf_lih_optimize, which runs the same molecule at the
# derived defaults. Two things it establishes that the other cases do not:
#
#   * a value set in the `optimization` group beats the derived one. The driver
#     sets its thresholds with set_derived_value (Drivers.hpp), so anything a deck
#     states wins; the values below are all tighter than what would be derived
#     from `dconv` (gtol 1e-4, xtol 1e-3, gradient_precision 1e-5), and the run
#     converges to a correspondingly smaller residual.
#
#   * the optimizer can be driven tighter than the default when the deck is
#     willing to pay for it. These are in fact the thresholds the retired in-SCF
#     `gopt` path used to impose on everyone; they are a fine *choice* and a poor
#     *default*, because at a looser `dconv` they sit on the gradient's own noise
#     floor and the optimizer grinds instead of converging.
#
# What this case has always really tested is the projection. MolOpt removes
# translations and rotations from the gradient before testing convergence
# (MolOpt::print_gradient reports both the projected gradient and the net force
# it took out). The raw gradient here carries a spurious net force of ~1.6e-4
# a.u., an identical dE/dz on both atoms; without the projection `max-g` never
# reaches `gtol` and the run burns every cycle at a geometry that stopped moving.
# `max_gradient` is the key that notices -- asserting the energy alone would not,
# since it is right either way. LiH is linear, so the projector must also cope
# with the vanishing rotation about the molecular axis.
#
# The start is 0.015 bohr inside the HF minimum.
#
# Run:   ./run.sh    (or: madqc --optimize --wf=scf scf_lih_optimize_tight.in)

optimization
    gtol                1e-5
    xtol                1e-5
    gradient_precision  1e-6
    maxiter             10
end

dft
    xc          hf
    protocol    [1e-4, 1e-6]
    dconv       1e-4
end

molecule
    units   atomic
    eprec   1e-6
    Li  0.0  0.0  0.0
    H   0.0  0.0  3.05
end
